/T (This method allows you to group data based on one or more columns. You can think of it as a powerful version of the SQL GROUP BY statement. First, you need to pass the column name on which you want to group the data. After that, you can use the grouped data and choose the column between which you want to compare this grouped data, and then select the aggregate function\( mean, sum, max, min, etc.. \). When you apply an aggregation function to grouped data without specifying a column, it will be applied to all the numeric columns in the DataFrame.)
